course: dictionary
lesson: 3050
title: Eastern: a word for direction
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Eastern is an adjective, a describing word. It tells you which part of a place you mean, or which way something faces. The eastern side of a place is the side nearest the east, where the sun comes up. «The empire was split into a western half ruled from Rome and an eastern half ruled from Constantinople.» Western is the opposite, so the words help each other: if western is one side, eastern is the other.
explain: Eastern can also describe the countries and cultures of Asia, especially East Asia, and it often has a capital E. This use is broad, so when you can, name the real country instead.
explain: Use the context to check your meaning. «The Phoenicians, sea-traders of the eastern Mediterranean, spread a 22-letter alphabet about 3,000 years ago.» The word Mediterranean tells you this is a sea, so eastern means the part of the sea nearest the east. Try swapping in east: the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Eastern means in, from or towards the east.
fact: The sun rises in the east, so the eastern sky is where the sun comes up.
fact: Places farther east see the sunrise earlier than places farther west.
fact: «Eastern Europe» and «eastern Canada» name the east part of a bigger area.
fact: With a capital E, «Eastern» can describe Asia and its cultures, as in «Eastern philosophy».
exercise: «The empire was split into a western half ruled from Rome and an eastern half ruled from Constantinople.» What does eastern mean in this sentence? | Towards the west | *The part of the empire on the east side | The part ruled by the sea | The part with the most cities
exercise: Which word means the opposite of eastern? | southern | *western | northern
exercise: «The sun rises in the eastern sky.» Where does the sun come up? | At midnight | In the south | In the west | *In the east
test: «Wheeled carts appeared about 5,500 years ago, in the Middle East and on the steppes of Eastern Europe.» What does Eastern Europe mean? | The west part of Europe | A very old city | A country called Eastern | *The east part of Europe
test: Why do places farther east see the sunrise earlier? | Because the sun is closer to them | *Because the sun rises in the east, so they get its light first | Because they have more clocks | Because the sun rises in the west first
exam: «The eastern coast of the USA is busy with ships.» What does eastern mean here? | The coast of Asia | *The coast on the east side of the USA | The coast on the west side of the USA | A coast that is very old
